{"id": "EUVD-2026-39902", "enisaUuid": "36d3d98a-4c76-39ad-ae1d-33209d074b85", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: mana: Guard mana_remove against double invocation\n\nIf PM resume fails (e.g., mana_attach() returns an error), mana_probe()\ncalls mana_remove(), which tears down the device and sets\ngd->gdma_context = NULL and gd->driver_data = NULL.\n\nHowever, a failed resume callback does not automatically unbind the\ndriver. When the device is eventually unbound, mana_remove() is invoked\na second time. Without a NULL check, it dereferences gc->dev with\ngc == NULL, causing a kernel panic.\n\nAdd an early return if gdma_context or driver_data is NULL so the second\ninvocation is harmless. Move the dev = gc->dev assignment after the\nguard so it cannot dereference NULL.", "datePublished": "2026-06-26T19:40:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:42:28", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/793bf1f4e469c51d0e39199823da5e1de85a2741", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ee85b75a72216c857c39457f6595709c4c9f856", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a1ddfd2c0b7a48e5239fadd2a24cc4bc2cda90e6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bbe5c3c570645a4ceb120979d3ee203a1583d775", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/50271d7ec95144d26808025b508f463780517d3c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-53297", "GHSA-43rv-4q7x-r3cg"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "080ab1b0-6c2f-3d3b-88be-d168f4307645", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "635096a86edb067d55a1e04b4a918f5c6dac0c51 <50271d7ec95144d26808025b508f463780517d3c"}, {"id": "10312bc8-2ae1-3041-80d1-df739592e934", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1b44596d-00d9-3c8c-922d-0f2cfaf614ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.33"}, {"id": "2ec738ab-9403-3767-9649-452c66199f57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "3c640b7a-622d-3ef2-a334-28898fb92475", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "635096a86edb067d55a1e04b4a918f5c6dac0c51 <bbe5c3c570645a4ceb120979d3ee203a1583d775"}, {"id": "56c25bfb-7e0e-3274-b3f4-7913c64ad130", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "635096a86edb067d55a1e04b4a918f5c6dac0c51 <793bf1f4e469c51d0e39199823da5e1de85a2741"}, {"id": "58a97e15-4c6b-30dd-a034-68cef224f35f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "683c06a7-8d72-39ba-b3d3-db05d2dbe3cc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "9fe912d5-07a2-3c06-8c37-101e29bda038", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "635096a86edb067d55a1e04b4a918f5c6dac0c51 <a1ddfd2c0b7a48e5239fadd2a24cc4bc2cda90e6"}, {"id": "c66e63aa-9a51-380e-a0e2-e3600aed436b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "635096a86edb067d55a1e04b4a918f5c6dac0c51 <8ee85b75a72216c857c39457f6595709c4c9f856"}, {"id": "e36c7a6f-daf5-3c91-b142-b6b4735132b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.10"}, {"id": "e56e85cf-1237-3151-807b-4415720fc8bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.16"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7cc38beb-1871-302d-833c-8f9838b055e3", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}